\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Completed finite searches. Four unresolved ten-point root cases split into 260 branches (240 closed), leaving 20 residual cases. Eighteen close in the residual table; two final whole-branch runs close the remainder. Thus the ten-point cover has \(280+292=572\) terminal UNSAT cases. Smaller sizes follow by the exact-size reduction.}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:runs}{{1}{4}{Completed finite searches. Four unresolved ten-point root cases split into 260 branches (240 closed), leaving 20 residual cases. Eighteen close in the residual table; two final whole-branch runs close the remainder. Thus the ten-point cover has \(280+292=572\) terminal UNSAT cases. Smaller sizes follow by the exact-size reduction}{table.1}{}}
